BT /F2 15 Tf 42 800 Td (Maximize Area Between Two Boundaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 42 777 Td (Practice Part A - Problem 5 | Python) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 751 Td (Task: Maximize min\(heights[left], heights[right]\) * \(right-left\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 741 Td (Move the pointer at the shorter wall because the shorter wall limits height.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 731 Td (def maxContainerArea\(heights\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 721 Td (left, right = 0, len\(heights\) - 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 711 Td (best = 0) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 701 Td (while left < right:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 691 Td (height = min\(heights[left], heights[right]\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 681 Td (best = max\(best, height * \(right-left\)\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 671 Td (if heights[left] <= heights[right]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 661 Td (left += 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 651 Td (else:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 641 Td (right -= 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 631 Td (return best) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 611 Td (print\(maxContainerArea\([1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]\)\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 591 Td (Output: 49) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 581 Td (Brute force is O\(n^2\) time. Two pointers are O\(n\) time and O\(1\) extra space.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 42 571 Td (The linear method scales much better for very large arrays.) Tj ET
